      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T21:08:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this patch is checked in aosp, and more partners will be impacted, so I would like to understand the above behavior is the one we expect before we proceed. Apologize if you have explained it in other meetings / conversations before.\n\nThe above behavior is what I interpreted from CLs in topic `angle_selection_refactor_1`. Since the default ANGLE apk is not taken out yet, we can put aside the question of \"ANGLE apk not available\". Would you mind checking if `persist.graphics.egl` is ANGLE, below behaviors are correct?\n\n\"default\": use ANGLE binary in /vendor.\n\"angle\": use ANGLE apk.\n\"native\": use ANGLE binary in /vendor. (EGL Loader.cpp will read persist.graphics.egl first before ro.hardware.egl)",
      "parentUuid": "12791325_47414829",
      "revId": "586cdf46ffad22d95476239ac2f16f505377d0a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e58cf7fb_66ca102a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1267775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T21:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the patches we submitted in internal master, right?\n\nIf \"default\" is used, nothing happens, EGL will load whatever it needs to load, meaning it looks up `persist.graphics.egl` first. If \"angle\" is used, it selects the ANGLE apk. If \"native\" is used, nothing happens, EGL will load whatever it needs to load.\n\nWithout this cherry-pick, our internal patches will be released to AOSP once U is released, this is just to make the code visible in advance so that I can talk with partners and point partners to meaningful code.",
      "parentUuid": "9931cd66_5004a56b",
      "revId": "586cdf46ffad22d95476239ac2f16f505377d0a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3995e9ec_bf4075fa",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1941946
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T21:50:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, when the change submitted in internal master, concerns in this ticket  http://b/280450222 hasn\u0027t been brought up yet, so I am asking extra questions here to understand behavior change is addressing per-app switch concerns in http://b/280450222. Specifically there was a concern when ANGLE is set as system driver, there was no way to know what the native driver is, and setting per-app switch to native does not force the app to use whatever native driver is shipped with the device.\n\nWith this change, we preserve the native driver name in `ro.hardware.egl`. However, since the EGL loader will looks up `persist.graphics.egl` before `ro.hardware.egl`, EGL loader will still load ANGLE for \"native\" and \"default\". We solved the problem of \"no way to know what the native driver is\", but in terms of actual loading, we are still loading ANGLE (read from \"persist.graphics.egl\"). As long as this is the expected behavior, I am good with it :)",
      "parentUuid": "e58cf7fb_66ca102a",
      "revId": "586cdf46ffad22d95476239ac2f16f505377d0a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
